# `cargo fuzz` build output and run output. The seed corpora under `corpus/` are
# checked in on purpose — they are the inputs the targets were last run against, and
# they are small; only what a run *grows* is ignored, and `cargo fuzz` writes new units
# to the first corpus directory it is given (a scratch one outside the tree), so a run
# does not touch the checked-in seeds.
target
artifacts
coverage
corpus/*-run/
